1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,180
How does Delta Lake work?

2
00:00:03,630 --> 00:00:08,010
A data lake is just files. Parquet files, sitting in cloud storage.

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:13,500
But if a job fails halfway through a write, it leaves half the files behind, and every reader sees broken data.

4
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:17,420
Delta Lake adds one thing: a transaction log.

5
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:22,820
Next to the data files sits a folder called _delta_log, holding numbered commit files.

6
00:00:22,970 --> 00:00:26,280
The log is the single source of truth for what the table contains.

7
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:30,510
When you write, Delta first writes the new Parquet files.

8
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:34,070
Then it adds the next commit to the log, in one atomic step.

9
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:37,190
If the job fails before the commit, the new files are simply ignored.

10
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:43,180
To read, Spark opens the log first, and replays the commits to get the list of current files.

11
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:45,880
Only those files are read. Nothing else.

12
00:00:47,330 --> 00:00:49,780
Parquet files are never edited in place.

13
00:00:49,930 --> 00:00:55,530
An update or delete writes a new file, and one commit marks the old file as removed and the new file as added.

14
00:00:56,980 --> 00:00:59,290
What if two writers commit at the same time?

15
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:02,780
Both try to create commit number three. Only one can win.

16
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:06,580
The other checks for conflicts, and retries as commit number four.

17
00:01:08,030 --> 00:01:12,520
Because old files are kept, and every commit is recorded, you can read the table as it was.

18
00:01:12,670 --> 00:01:17,040
VERSION AS OF 1 gives you the table exactly as it looked back then.

19
00:01:18,490 --> 00:01:23,660
Every ten commits, Delta writes a checkpoint: one Parquet file that summarizes the log so far.

20
00:01:23,810 --> 00:01:26,490
Readers start from the latest checkpoint, so they stay fast.

21
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:31,770
Files, plus a log. That is Delta Lake.

